{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the new moon.</b> On the first of the month, like 'tomorrow is the new moon.'" "<b>The third.</b> Because they were taken captive, and freed, and converted. And thus our Sages taught: the convert, and the captive woman, and the maidservant who were redeemed, and converted, and freed — must wait three months." "<b>On this day.</b> That they journeyed from Rephidim on the first of the month of Sivan, which was on the second day of the week — this is according to the Rabbans. As is established in chapter Rabbi Akiva: that the giving of the Torah was on the Sabbath, according to all opinions. And the Rabbans say: it was given on the sixth of the month. If so, the first of Sivan was on the second day of the week, and Iyar of that year was full (i.e., thirty days). And if you ask: if so, we find seven weeks and one day from Passover to Atzeret — one may answer: they were not commanded regarding the count until after entry. (i.e., the morrow of the Sabbath)" "<b>On this day they came to the wilderness of Sinai.</b> Rabbi Levi said: a parable — to a king's son who recovered from his illness. His tutor said: let him go to the escuela — in the vernacular, meaning: a house where young children are taught."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "Resolved the abbreviations א״כ as 'if so,' א״ת as 'and if you ask,' י״ל as 'one may answer,' ד״ה as 'i.e.' The parenthetical '(i.e., the morrow of the Sabbath)' is a conjectural resolution of the final opaque abbreviation in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:42.928678997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}